Single-database configuration for Flask.

Run these from the `backend/` directory with `FLASK_APP=main.py`:

    flask db upgrade                       # apply migrations (also run by deploy.sh)
    flask db migrate -m "describe change"  # create a new migration after editing models

Do not run `flask db init`; this directory already exists.

Rules:
- Schema changes only through Alembic, with a single head (`flask db heads`).
- No raw-SQL or one-off database scripts. A data fix is an Alembic data migration; data every install
  needs is an idempotent upsert in `flask seed`.
- A development database built by `create_all` has no Alembic revision: delete it, or stamp it first.

The production upgrade order and the development-database recipe are in
docs/infrastructure_and_devops.md, section 8.
